* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13g2-vco-kvco-table (issue #97, the SG13G2 twin of
* sg13cmos5l-vco-kvco-table, issue #23/Part of #16)
*
* Open-loop VCO frequency-vs-VCTRL sweep at a fixed band-select code and PVT
* corner. ../testbench/run.sh sweeps @VCTRL@/@B0V@/@B1V@ over the campaign's
* own matrix and substitutes @CORNER_MOS@ (cornerMOShv.lib section: mos_tt/
* mos_ss/mos_ff), @CORNER_RES@ (cornerRES.lib section: res_typ/res_wcs/
* res_bcs), @CORNER_CAP@ (cornerCAP.lib section: cap_typ/cap_bcs/cap_wcs --
* new relative to the SG13CMOS5L sibling, see ../corners/matrix.md "Why
* XCDECAP is kept, not stripped, here" for why this axis exists on this
* PDK) and @TEMP@ (degC), per ../corners/matrix.md's 3-bundle PVT convention
* (see that file for why a 3-bundle subset, not the full
* 5(mos)x3(res)x3(cap)x3(temp) cross product). @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ are also
* substituted by run.sh -- ngspice's `.lib`/`.include` netlist parser does
* not expand shell/OS environment variables (SG13CMOS5L sibling issue #43),
* so the corner-lib path below must be a real filesystem path by the time
* ngspice parses it.
*
* `.include`s the frozen ../netlist-snapshots/vco.spice DIRECTLY (unlike the
* SG13CMOS5L sibling, this record does not derive a local XCDECAP-stripped
* copy -- see ../corners/matrix.md), instantiates the real `vco` subckt with
* ideal DC sources on VCTRL/B0/B1/VDD_VCO, and measures the CLK output's
* steady-state period via ngspice `.meas trig/targ` between two later
* rising-edge crossings (skipping the ring's own startup transient).

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerCAP.lib @CORNER_CAP@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include @DUT@

Vvctrl vctrl 0 dc @VCTRL@
Vb0 b0 0 dc @B0V@
Vb1 b1 0 dc @B1V@
Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
Vsub sub! 0 dc 0

Xvco vctrl b0 b1 clk vdd 0 vco

* Breaks the ring's own node symmetry so ngspice's transient solver does not
* sit at the (unstable, but numerically exact) all-equal-nodes equilibrium
* indefinitely -- a real ring self-starts from any physical noise/mismatch;
* this is the same role a deliberate mismatch or a noise source plays in a
* real self-starting ring, applied as an explicit .ic since this compact
* model does not inject its own transient noise. Same mechanism and same
* probed node (xvco.ring1) as the SG13CMOS5L sibling -- this port shares the
* identical 5-stage ring topology and node names.
.ic v(xvco.ring1)=0.5

.tran 20p 40n

.control
run
meas tran per1 trig v(clk) val=1.65 rise=3 targ v(clk) val=1.65 rise=4
print per1
.endc
.end
